<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Andaman and Nicobar Islands, 2024</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Andaman and Nicobar Islands, 2024&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;The Time Is: 1 August, 2024, &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;00:00 Zulu/06:00 Nicobar Islands Time&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable as the Peoples Republic of China (PRC) Only&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;This is an Amphibious/Cargo Mission Scenario&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Thanks to Sanyr1320 &amp;amp;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;AndrewJ for&amp;nbsp;their feedback and contributions&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;2&amp;nbsp;Days&amp;nbsp;Duration &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Background: &lt;/STRONG&gt;The 572 islands of Andaman and Nicobar Islands were taking on increasing strategic importance in the early portion of the Twenty-first Century. The northernmost part of the archipelago is a mere 22 nautical miles away from (a PRC friendly) Myanmar, and Indira Point, the southernmost point in the islands, is only 90 nautical miles from Indonesia. These islands dominate the Bay of Bengal and the Six Degree and Ten Degree channels through which more than 60,000 commercial vessels traverse each year!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Among the nine (9) major bottlenecks that control entry to this region&amp;nbsp;is the Malacca Strait. The Andaman and Nicobar Islands lie in this strategically important zone, meaning that India, with its growing naval capabilities, could play a significant role in controlling access. With this in mind, India has developed the Andaman and Nicobar Command (ANC), India’s only Joint Forces Command. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;India has begun a process of expanding the bases in this area. This scenario assumes that India has expanded the INS Baaz base on Great Nicobar Island and INS Kohassa on North Andaman Island. These ANC bases will be&amp;nbsp;expanded to take multirole and MPA aircraft. Other port facilities&amp;nbsp;are planned to be&amp;nbsp;expanded for destroyers and one&amp;nbsp;may even be expanded to support carriers.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Peoples Republic of China (PRC) in the meantime had been busy cultivating support across the region, including working on basing in Myanmar. In the end, the unrest in Myanmar (and some mistrust) kept the PRC from fully developing bases in the county, but the Military junta was more than happy to allow the PLA(N) and PLA(AF) overflight rights to enter the Bay of Bengal. In 2023 and the summer of 2024 increasing confrontations between PRC MPA/H-6 aircraft and India multirole aircraft occurred over the Bay of Bengal. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Tensions in the disputed eastern Ladakh region began to escalate in June, 2024 with tens of thousands of troops and artillery dispatched by both sides by the end of the month. The night of July 3rd-4th thousands of PLA troops infiltrated behind the Indian Army’s Patrolling Point 14 in the Galwan Valley. In the predawn hours’ illumination rounds flared over Indian positions as search lights blinded the troops. Within minutes thousands of PLA troops began attacking the post. IAF aircraft were called in for support and a battalion sized task force of the Indian 16th Bihar Regiment was dispatched. By noon the post was overrun with no prisoners taken and the Bihar Regiment was heavily engaged. The next day PLA forces crossed the Line of Control (LAC) into the Depsang Plains in force. IAF and PLAAF engaged in dogfights over Jammu and Kashmir and artillery engaged in counter battery duels&amp;nbsp;in just about every disputed area.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Over the next few weeks, the conflict deepened with Pakistan joining in. The United States, United Kingdom and Israel officially stayed neutral but began to both resupply Indian forces and provide intelligence. The PRC refused any overture to end the Himalayan conflict and vetoed any Security Council Resolutions with respect to the conflict. In Mid-July the Indians announced a blockade of the Malacca Straits to any PRC, or PRC allied nation, and enforced it using the newly built-up bases of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands (ANC). The PRC warned India to cease these actions, a threat which was quick rebuffed by New Delhi. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On July 26th&amp;nbsp;two PLA(N) carrier task forces built around the carriers Shandong and Liaoning, as well as an amphibious force centered on the LHD Hainan departed the Hainan Island naval bases headed for the Straits. Lloyds of London and other maritime insurers declared the Straits of Malacca to be a war zone and tripled the rate for any vessels transiting the area. Soon merchants were diverting south of Java to safer waters. Shandong, suffering some engine difficulties falls behind by about 18 hours.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Myanmar, has banned PLA forces from basing on their territory but has allowed overflights by PLA(AF) and PLA(N) aircraft. Forewarned of the PLA(N) actions, by western intelligence satellites (and western media tracking the PLA(N) carrier group), India began to deploy additional naval assets and both of their carriers to the Sea of Bengal. The stage was set for the world’s first carrier clash since the closing months of World War Two.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Mission:&lt;/STRONG&gt; As commander of the PLA(N) forces you are tasked with taking Great Nicobar Island by amphibious operation (Cargo Mission). Your carriers are to support the amphibious operations and if necessary, engage Indian naval forces. You will have support from H-6K "God of War" Badgers and AEW aircraft, deployed to southern China and allowed to overfly Myanmar.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Notes: &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Make sure Special/Popup Messages are enabled.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;I have set&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;EM&gt;SOME&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; Side Doctrine for the PLA(N) side, mainly ASMs and torpedoes. Doctrine is fully set for the Indian A/I. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Your two regiments of H-6Ks are at the Guiping/Mengshu Air Base&amp;nbsp;along with two AEW aircraft and 18 HY-6U tankers. Again, these aircraft can overfly Myanmar.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Each aircraft had a random 30 percent&amp;nbsp;chance of being down for maint.&amp;nbsp;You choose your carrier (JD-15, J-15) and cargo (LCAC/Helio) loadouts for your aircraft. I did load out the H-6Ks with loadouts due to the long loadout times and with maximum flexibility in mission. &lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;FONT color=red&gt;You can either alter in the Scenrio Editor to your tastes or change the loadouts for the second mission.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; Carrier Helios (AEW/ASW) do not have quick turn arounds, the ASW&amp;nbsp;screen Helios do, and &lt;FONT color=red&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;EM&gt;you can adjust&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Three of your submarines teleport&amp;nbsp;2 seconds into&amp;nbsp;the scenario, I have set up missions for them to help right after they teleport. &lt;U&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT color=red&gt;If you don’t like the missions, adjust or delete them&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/U&gt;. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;If your amphibious vessels remain within the operations zone off Great Nicobar Island for six (6) hours you receive Victory Points (VPs). &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=black&gt;No not delete the locked "Amphibious Operations" Reference Points."&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;If your land forces are on Great Nicobar Island, within the reference points, for five (5) hours you capture Port Campbell and for six (6) hours INS Baaz Air Base. Both are worth VPs for the PLA(N). &lt;FONT color=black&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Do not delete the locked Reference points on Great Nicobar Island&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;. I suggest you don’t destroy the base as it could be used to support operations.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You only receive and loose VPs for the destruction of High Value Units (HVU; aircraft carriers and the LHD).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Your Liaoning CSG and Amphibious groups have just replenished and their AOEs are low on fuel. A large replenishment group has just departed Johor Port, Malaysia topped off (if necessary to support operations). Shandong CSG put into Johor to effect engine&amp;nbsp;repairs and was fully fueled in that port.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Scoring: 0 points = Disaster and 12,000 a Triumph&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Built under C:MO Build 1147.25 Database DB3000 v487&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;A Delta File is provided for deep rebuilds.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
